A||||4||sqoach||Brakes rubbing pretty bad||||11||
Z||000000||sqoach||07-07-2001||11:12 PM||||It seems as though the caliper piston is not releasing all the way. You can hear it rubbing all the way around. Plus, the brakes aren't working very good. It's not stopping as good as it's suppose to. Does this mean my calipers need rebuilt? I was low on brake fluid, but would it have that much of an impact on the performance of the brakes? Any ideas? The brake pads are still pretty good.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumsig.JPG">      <BR>84 SE (FOR SALE)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)(take it off my hands for $50)<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE sometime in this summer)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)||||reg||11
Z||000001||Tigger||07-07-2001||11:49 PM||||Good chance the caliper slides are bunged up.  Try to move the caliper back and forth on the slides by hand, if it doesn't move very good that's your problem and the calipers may not have be rebuilt.<P>You can get the new rubber seals/guides and the red grease at any auto parts store.||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||07-08-2001||07:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tigger:<BR><B>Good chance the caliper slides are bunged up.  Try to move the caliper back and forth on the slides by hand, if it doesn't move very good that's your problem and the calipers may not have be rebuilt.<P>You can get the new rubber seals/guides and the red grease at any auto parts store.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>How easily are they suppose to move? I remember that I could move them. I have a feeling it's something to do with the piston. I'll take a better look at it tomorrow.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||07-08-2001||10:09 PM||||Caliper should slide back and forth easy with one hand-light force, should travel 1/8" or so depending on pad wear.<P>If it turns out to be the piston, rebuilding instructions are in the Haynes manual.  Might be able to find info here in a search.||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||07-09-2001||08:22 AM||||Yes the calipers should slide easly. It's only 6 bucks for caliper slide grease the hard part is doing it. ALL of my Fieros have had frozen calipers and bleeder valves  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> ||||reg||1
